{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-1","title":"John 11:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ raises Lazarus, four days buried. 45 Many Jews believe. 47 The high priests and Pharisees gather a council against Christ. 49 Caiaphas prophesies. 54 Jesus hides himself. 55 At the passover they enquire after him, and lay wait for him.</p>\n<p>Now.The raising of Lazarus from the dead, being a work of Christ beyond measure great, the most stupendous of all he had hitherto performed, and beyond all others calculated to evince his Divine majesty, was therefore purposely recorded by the Evangelist John; while it was omitted by the other Evangelists, probably, as Grotius supposes, because they wrote their histories during the life of Lazarus, and they did not mention him for fear of exciting the malice of the Jews against him; as we find from ch. 12:10, that they sought to put him to death, that our Lord might not have such a monument of his power and goodness remaining in the land.</p>\n<p>was sick. 3,6; Ge 48:1; 2Ki 20:1-12; Ac 9:37 Lazarus. 5,11; 12:2,9,17; Lu 16:20-25 Bethany. 12:1; Mt 21:17; Mr 11:1 Mary. Lu 10:38-42</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-2","title":"John 11:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>that Mary. 12:3; Mt 26:6,7; Mr 14:3 anointed. Lu 7:37,38</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-3","title":"John 11:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>he. 1,5; 13:23; Ge 22:2; Ps 16:3; Php 2:26,27; 2Ti 4:20; Heb 12:6,7 Jas 5:14,15; Re 3:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-4","title":"John 11:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>This. 9:3; Mr 5:39-42; Ro 11:11 for. 40; 9:24; 12:28; 13:31,32; Php 1:11; 1Pe 4:11,14 that. 2:11; 5:23; 8:54; 13:31,32; 17:1,5,10; Php 1:20; 1Pe 1:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-5","title":"John 11:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>loved. 8,36; 15:9-13; 16:27; 17:26</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-6","title":"John 11:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>he abode. Ge 22:14; 42:24; 43:29-31; 44:1-5; 45:1-5; Isa 30:18; 55:8,9 Mt 15:22-28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-7","title":"John 11:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Let. 10:40-42; Lu 9:51; Ac 15:36; 20:22-24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-8","title":"John 11:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>the Jews. 10:31,39; Ps 11:1-3; Mt 16:21-23; Ac 21:12,13 and goest. Ac 20:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-9","title":"John 11:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>Are. 9:4; Lu 13:31-33 he stumbleth not. 12:35; Pr 3:23; Jer 31:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-10","title":"John 11:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Ps 27:2; Pr 4:18,19; Ec 2:14; Jer 13:16; 20:11; 1Jo 2:10,11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-11","title":"John 11:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>he saith. 3:29; 15:13-15; Ex 33:11; 2Ch 20:7; Isa 41:8; Jas 2:23 sleepeth. 13; De 31:16; Da 12:2; Mt 9:24; Mr 5:39; Ac 7:60; 1Co 15:18,51 1Th 4:14,15; 5:10 awake. 43,44; 5:25-29; Da 12:2; 1Co 15:34; Eph 5:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-14","title":"John 11:14","author":"R. A. 