"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-43","title":"John 11:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>Lazarus. 1Ki 17:21,22; 2Ki 4:33-36; Mr 4:41; Lu 7:14,15; Ac 3:6,12; 9:34,40</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-44","title":"John 11:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>he that. 25,26; 5:21,25; 10:30; Ge 1:3; 1Sa 2:6; Ps 33:9; Eze 37:3-10; Ho 13:14 Ac 20:9-12; Php 3:21; Re 1:18 bound.\"Swathed about with rollers\" or bandages, [keiria ,] long strips of linen, a few inches in breadth, brought round the [sindon ,] or sheet of linen in which the corpse was involved, and by which the [aromata,] or spices, were kept in contact with the flesh. In reply to sceptical objections, it is sufficient to observe, that he who could raise Lazarus from the dead, could, with a much less exertion of power, have so loosened or removed the bandages of his feet and legs as to have rendered it practicable for him to come forth. Tittman well observes, that Lazarus was restored not only to life but also to health, as appears from the alacrity of his motion; and this would constitute a new miracle.</p>\n<p>20:5,7 Loose. 39; Mr 5:43; Lu 7:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-45","title":"John 11:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>Jews. 19,31; 2:23; 10:41; 12:9-11,17-19,42</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-46","title":"John 11:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>5:15,16; 9:13; 12:37; Lu 16:30,31; Ac 5:25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-47","title":"John 11:47","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":47,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":47},"content":"<p>gathered. Ps 2:2-4; Mt 26:3; 27:1,2; Mr 14:1; Lu 22:2; Ac 4:5,6,27,28; 5:21 What. 12:19; Ac 4:16,17; 5:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-48","title":"John 11:48","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":48,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":48},"content":"<p>we let. Ac 5:28,38-40 all. 1:7; Lu 8:12; 11:52; 1Th 2:15,16 and the. De 28:50-68; Da 9:26,27; Zec 13:7,8; 14:1,2; Mt 21:40-42; 22:7 Mt 23:35-38; 27:25; Lu 19:41-44; 21:20-24; 23:28-31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-49","title":"John 11:49","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":49,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":49},"content":"<p>Caiaphas. 18:13,14; Lu 3:2; Ac 4:6 Ye. 7:48,49; Pr 26:12; Isa 5:20-23; 1Co 1:20; 2:6; 3:18,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-50","title":"John 11:50","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":50,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":50},"content":"<p>48; 18:14; 19:12; Lu 24:46; Ro 3:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-51","title":"John 11:51","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":51,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":51},"content":"<p>being. Ex 28:30; Jud 20:27,28; 1Sa 23:9; 28:6 he prophesied. Nu 22:28; 24:2,14-25; Mt 7:22,23; 1Co 13:2; 2Pe 2:15-17 that Jesus. 10:15; Isa 53:5-8; Da 9:26; Mt 20:28; Ro 3:25,26; 2Co 5:21; Ga 3:13 Ga 4:4,5; 1Pe 2:24; 3:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-52","title":"John 11:52","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":52,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":52},"content":"<p>not. 1:29; 12:32; Ps 22:15,27; 72:19; Isa 49:6; Lu 2:32; Ro 3:29; 1Jo 2:2 Re 5:9; 7:9,10 gather. 10:16; Ge 49:10; Ps 102:22,23; Isa 11:10-12; 49:18; 55:5; 56:8; 60:4 Mt 25:31-34; Eph 1:9,10; 2:14-22; Col 1:20-23 the children. Ho 1:10; Ac 18:10; Ro 4:17; 8:29,30; 9:25,26; Eph 1:5; 3:11 2Th 2:13,14 that were. Eze 11:16,17; 34:12; Eph 2:14-17; Jas 1:1; 1Pe 1:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-53","title":"John 11:53","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":53,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":53},"content":"<p>from. Ne 4:16; 13:21; Ps 113:2; Mt 16:21; 22:46 they. 47; Ps 2:2; 31:13; 71:10; Mr 3:6; Ac 5:33; 9:23 put. 12:10; Ps 109:4,5; Jer 38:4,15; Mt 26:59; Mr 14:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-54","title":"John 11:54","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":54,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":54},"content":"<p>walked. 4:1-3; 7:1; 10:40; 18:20 went. 7:4,10,13 Ephraim.Ephraim appears to be the same city which is called Ephrain, 2 Ch 13:19 (where see the Note), and Ephron, Jos 15:9, which was situated eight miles north of Jerusalem, near Bethel, and apparently between that city and Jericho. Accordingly we find that a desert, or wilderness, extended from Jericho to Bethel (Jos 16:1), called the wilderness of Bethaven (Jos 18:12), in which Joshua and the Israelites slew the inhabitants of Ai. (Jos 8:24.)</p>\n<p>2Sa 13:23; 2Ch 13:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-55","title":"John 11:55","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":55,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":55},"content":"<p>passover. 2:13; 5:1; 6:4; Ex 12:11-14 before. 7:8-10; 12:1; Ezr 3:1-6; Ne 8:1-12 to purify. 2:6; Ge 35:2; Ex 19:10,14,15; Nu 9:6; 1Sa 16:5; 2Ch 30:17-20 Job 1:5; Ps 26:6; Ac 24:18; 1Co 11:28; Heb 9:13,14; Jas 4:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-56","title":"John 11:56","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":56,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":56},"content":"<p>8; 7:11; 11:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-11-57","title":"John 11:57","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":11,"verseStart":57,"chapterEnd":11,"verseEnd":57},"content":"<p>had. 5:16-18; 8:59; 9:22; 10:39; Ps 109:4</p>"}]}